    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48327" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tīfāta</span></b> ,
		ōrum, n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a mountain ridge north of Capua</i>, now
				<i>Monte Maddaloni</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 7, 29,
				6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">23, 36,
			1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">26, 5, 4</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Vell.
				2, 25, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 12, 487</span></i>; <i><span class="en">13, 219</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				366</span></i>. — Hence, ‡ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tīfātīnus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Tifata</i>, <i>Tifatinian</i>: DIANA, Inscr. Rein. cl. 6, n. 91;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Murat. 446, 4</span></i>.</div>
